{"name":"Nature Apricot","hex":"#feb7a5","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"nature","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The way things are, the totality of all things in the physical universe and their order, especially the physical world in contrast to spiritual realms and flora and fauna as distinct from human conventions, art, and technology.","The particular way someone or something is, especially\nThe essential or innate characteristics of a person or thing which will always tend to manifest, especially in contrast to specific contexts, reason, religious duty, upbringing, and personal pretense or effort."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To endow with natural qualities."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nature"},{"term":"apricot","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A round sweet and juicy stone fruit, resembling peach or plum in taste, with a yellow-orange flesh, lightly fuzzy skin and a large seed inside.","The apricot tree, Prunus armeniaca."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a pale yellowish-orange colour, like that of an apricot."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/apricot"}],"entries":[{"title":"Nature","blocks":[{"text":"Nature, in the broadest sense, is the physical world or universe. In this general sense nature refers to the laws, elements and phenomena of the physical world, including life. Although humans are part of nature, human activity or humans as a whole are often described as at times at odds, or outright separate and even superior to nature."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/06/Startrails_above_Gunung_Bromo_-_Indonesia.jpg/330px-Startrails_above_Gunung_Bromo_-_Indonesia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nature","wikidata":"Q7860"},{"title":"Apricot","blocks":[{"text":"An apricot is a fruit, or the tree that bears the fruit, of several species in the genus Prunus. Usually an apricot is from the species Prunus armeniaca, but the fruits of the other species in Prunus sect. Armeniaca are also called apricots. In 2023, world production of apricots was 3.7 million tonnes, led by Turkey with 20% of the total."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/Apricot_and_cross_section.jpg/330px-Apricot_and_cross_section.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apricot","wikidata":"Q3733836"},{"title":"Apricot (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Apricot is a light yellowish-orangish color that is similar to the color of apricots. However, it is paler than actual apricots."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apricot_(color)","wikidata":"Q1324818"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/70/The_Blue_Marble%2C_AS17-148-22727.jpg/500px-The_Blue_Marble%2C_AS17-148-22727.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/70/The_Blue_Marble%2C_AS17-148-22727.jpg/1280px-The_Blue_Marble%2C_AS17-148-22727.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/70/The_Blue_Marble%2C_AS17-148-22727.jpg/500px-The_Blue_Marble%2C_AS17-148-22727.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Blue Marble, which is a famous view of the Earth, taken in 1972 by the crew of Apollo 17","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AThe_Blue_Marble%2C_AS17-148-22727.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/40/Tectonic_plate_boundaries.png/500px-Tectonic_plate_boundaries.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/40/Tectonic_plate_boundaries.png/500px-Tectonic_plate_boundaries.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&ut